From c3e3fa19dd641964442985774a3bdfd1cd25e6ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baricco <38298051+Baricco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:11:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] goodixgf: add driver for Goodix 27c6:5125/5135
 (ChicagoHS, 80x64)

Image device on top of SIGFM for the Goodix ST411SEC sensors found in
Huawei/Honor laptops: PSK provisioning, TLS-PSK channel (mbedtls), FDT
finger detection, 12-bit image unpacking. Based on the goodixgf driver
by Rockytkg, with:

- ridge image pipeline (DoG band-pass + CLAHE, fresh no-finger baseline
  next to each touch, gain-ghost regression) and a ridge-contrast quality
  gate; the old flat-field/unsharp output let sensor fixed-pattern noise
  dominate weak touches;
- 0x80/0x82 "reverse" finger-down handled as a touch;
- up to 30 enroll frames, coverage convergence by diversity check;
- no bundled vendor firmware: version is only compared, never flashed.

27c6:5125 removed from the unsupported list; hwdb regenerated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
